CLASSIFICATION: INFRASTRUCTURE DEADLINE ONLY.  The launch-witness budget decides
when a launch is declared DEAD.  No gate, band, threshold, cap or label is
touched and no gate reads it.  LA.3, the strict-minority guard, is left exactly
as frozen and now re-checks a derived value.

WHAT CHANGED: one token becomes a derivation.
  LAUNCH_BUDGET_S=__D8G_UNFROZEN__WITNESS_BUDGET
  -> LAUNCH_BUDGET_S=$(python3 ... floor((TMO-1)/2) ...) + a D4S_ echo of it
TMO is already derived at the cap assertion from the registered cap and rank
count, so the budget now descends from that same single number.  A literal would
create a second number that can drift from the first.
THE FORM: floor((TMO-1)/2) is the largest integer STRICTLY below TMO/2 for both
parities.  Largest is a SAFETY choice: this clock decides when a launch is
called dead, so every second removed from it is added to the chance of killing a
HEALTHY run merely slow to reach its first iteration.  A genuinely dead
container is caught by the container-state reader, not by this clock.

FINDING 1 -- TWO OF THE SIX QUOTED CEILINGS WOULD HAVE ABORTED.
The brief quoted 352 / 393 / 719 / 915 / 1526 / 1606 s.  They ARE reproducible
from TMO -- they are TMO/2 rounded -- but LA.3 is STRICT (0 < b < t/2) and a
rounded half is not below its own half.  Measured against the guard:
  arm    TMO    TMO/2   derived  LA.3(derived)  quoted  LA.3(quoted)
  L1-P    705   352.5     352    PASS             352   PASS
  L2-P    786   393.0     392    PASS             393   *** ABORT ***
  L3-P   1439   719.5     719    PASS             719   PASS
  A2-P   1829   914.5     914    PASS             915   *** ABORT ***
  F2-P   3053  1526.5    1526    PASS            1526   PASS
  F2-S   3213  1606.5    1606    PASS            1606   PASS
  (the -S arms share their -P caps; all PASS on the derived value)
*** HARD-CODING THE QUOTED TABLE WOULD HAVE ABORTED L2-P AND A2-P AT LA.3 THE
FIRST TIME THEY RAN -- after staging, after the image and row checks, at the
launch itself.  The ruling to derive rather than hard-code prevented a failure
nobody had predicted. ***

FINDING 2 -- THE WITNESS IS NOT THE MPIRUN LINE, AND THE HEADROOM IS THIN.
The design note at line 4 says the budget is "MEASURED by the first arm's
D4S_MPIRUN_EPOCH line".  The witness the CODE waits for is
  LAUNCH_WITNESS_RE = ^ExecutionTime =        (line 588)
-- THE FIRST SOLVER ITERATION -- with ^Time = as the decomposePar DECOY and
^Running Primal Solver as corroborator.  D4S_MPIRUN_EPOCH is deliberately built
to match none of the log readers (lines 470-477), so it cannot be the witness.
The budget must cover container start + TensorFlow import + DASolver
construction + decomposePar + ONE ITERATION.
  MEASURED TONIGHT, A3GC L3, 99,840 cells, 4 ranks, this box:
    launch 22:15:33Z -> first ExecutionTime ~22:19-22:20Z = ~270-290 s at load
    26-32; the earlier attempt at load 37-70 took ~370 s to the same point.
    The four TensorFlow banners landed ~60-70 s in, and THAT COST IS
    MESH-INDEPENDENT.
  D8G L1 is 5,568 cells -- 18x smaller -- so its mesh read and decomposePar are
  near-instant, but the import is not.  Against L1-P's derived 352 s the
  headroom is real but THINNER THAN IT LOOKS, and it CANNOT be widened: 352 is
  the ceiling LA.3 permits at a 46.977 core-min cap.  If an arm ever fails LA
  with a healthy container, read this paragraph first.

